From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/cix: dptx: clear the ELD when the EDID read fails

When the EDID read fails, get_modes keeps the ELD of the previous sink.
get_eld then reports audio formats that the new sink may not support.
Clear the EDID property, which also clears the ELD.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_drm.c
@@ -332,6 +332,9 @@
 	}
 
 	if (!edid) {
+		/* Drop the ELD of the previous sink. */
+		drm_connector_update_edid_property(connector, NULL);
+
 		mode = drm_dp_downstream_mode(connector->dev, dp->dpcd,
 					      dp->downstream_ports);
 		if (mode) {
